ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG1", "Geysers - The area up to the first boss has multiple Geysers, these need to be avoided as the damage from these, both when they are active or inactive is high. The AoE damage they produce is larger than the area of water so stay well away from them.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG2", "Plants & Death Hoppers - The plants here do damage, simply avoid them as you move through the area. The Death Hoppers do a poison spit which doesn't hit too hard, these adds can be stacked with the other smaller adds and killed quite easily.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG3", "Sul-Xan Reaver - This mob wields its 2 handed weapon into the ground which will apply a debuff on its target if not dodged. It also produces the 'Earthquake' ability when its stamps it foot, which produces a large poison AoE that does damage and produces Stranglers.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG4", "Sul-Xan Soulweaver - This mob casts shields on allies it is near. Either focus this add down fast first or have the off-tank take it away from the other adds and deal with it separately. It also places AoE circles on 3 players of the group who will need to move away from everyone else before they explode.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG5", "Sul-Xan Bloodseeker - This add jumps repeatedly which makes it harder to tank, keep taunt on this as tank. It doesn't hit too hard but as it is an archer its cone can hit the group with it jumps making it difficult to keep it facing in the correct direction.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG6", "1st Mini Bosses - Once you reach the Haj Mota, follow the path to the left and you will find the 1st Mini Bosses. Basks in Snakes needs to be turned away from the group and tanked next to the Giant Snake. Throughout the fight a large number of smaller snakes will appear & can be burned in the group AoE. The Giant Snake needs it bite blocking and interrupting when it curls up.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG7", "1st Boss - Oaxiltse - Savage Blitz - The boss targets the furthest player away and charges them, you can dodge this attack if timed correctly or block the incoming damage.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG8", "1st Boss - Noxious Sludge - 2 players will be spat at by the boss, their screen will turn orange and they need to find a clean pool to cleanse in. The pool will then turn green and produce Death Hoppers which need to be killed fast so as not to get overwhelmed by too many of them as they all do the Fetid Spit attack.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG9", "1st Boss - Noxious Puddle - Failure to cleanse the Noxious Sludge quickly will result in you dropping Noxious Puddles in the group causing damage to other players.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG10", "1st Boss - Stomp - The boss produces lines of fire each time he stomps his foot on the floor. He does this 3 times is quick succession, make sure to avoid the damage from this attack.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG11", "1st Boss - Meteor Crash - Meteors will hit the ground from time to time, these can generally be avoided as you can walk out of the incoming AoE, otherwise simply block them.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG12", "1st Boss - Ravenous Chomp & Blistering Smash - The boss will bite you, this is a heavy attack and needs blocking, it can't be interrupted. He does a 2 handed smash that leaves an AoE on the ground that needs avoiding.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG13", "1st Boss - Havocrel Annihilator - The main boss will start screaming and a large circle appears to indicate where the new add will appear. The add spawns at 95%, 75%, 50% & 25% and must be taunted by the off-tank and taken away from the main boss to prevent them both enraging. Keep the main boss outside of the Annihilators permanent gold AoE.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG14", "Havocrel Annihilator - Hack - This hit can be blocked or dodged and should only ever hit the off-tank.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG15", "Havocrel Annihilator - Sunhammer - This is a very heavy overhead swing from the Havocrel which will oneshot you if it hits without being dodged. It will also cause meteors to drop on 2 players which must be blocked.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG16", "Havocrel Annihilator - Cinder Cleave - The add will turn and target a player with a large cone AoE. That player can move the cone out of the group and dodge roll the hit from the attack but anyone inside the cone will still take a DoT regardless of dodging or blocking that will need cleansing.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG17", "Havocrel Annihilator - Ashen Wounds - A DoT caused by the Annihilator that can persist even after he has been killed.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG18", "Havocrel Annihilator - Chains - The add will randomly chain 2 players into him which puts them at risk of being hit by the other heavy attacks.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG19", "Next Adds - After defeating Oaxiltse the following rooms to the next boss contain the same adds as you have already seen as well as a new Havocrel adds, the Havocrel Butcher & Havorcrel Barbarian.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG20", "Havocrel Butcher - It shoots out a Fiery Eruption ring when it stamps its foot doing Ignite DoT damage to anyone in the area. The uppercut heavy attack, that should focus the tank, can be dodged. The tank should also face the 3 fire lines that come off this add away from the group.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG21", "Havocrel Barbarian - This is a hard add to tank as it moves quickly from player to player and will likely oneshot if the very fast dual wield Hasted Assault attack is not blocked.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG22", "2nd Boss - Flame-Herald Bahsei - The boss will lift his sword and cast Skull Salvo shooting mini meteors at the group, this must be interrupted. 3 whirlwinds come fromm the boss and should hit the tank as this Sickle Strike attack causes the Deaths Touch curse, this can not be dodged.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG23", "2nd Boss - Cursed Ground - Chains will rise from the ground and explode, this should hit the furthest 2 players away from the boss so can be placed outside the group. This will casue the 2 players to be cursed with Death Touch.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG24", "2nd Boss - Death Touch - Players get cursed from Cursed Ground chains or Sickle Strike and will glow blue, they will explode after 8 seconds shooting out more curses in random driections that will kill other players. You must take this out of the group so everyone can be ready to avoid the whirlwind curses and the final explosion.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG25", "2nd Boss - Tank Position - The boss will shoot 3 curses out across the floor, these don't want to hit the group so the tank can face the boss away from the group, using the far left corner can help, or the centre and rotating around as the boss health decreases.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG26", "2nd Boss - Archers - These appear at the edges of the area, they need to be interrupted to prevent them charging a heavy attack on players. Chain them into the group AoE and burn them or simply burn at range.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG27", "2nd Boss - Fire Waves & Meteors & Burning Spectres - Both waves of fire and fire meteors will be in the arena, they do not hit too hard can can generally be avoided. Burning Spectres will fly across the arena & can't be taunted, they should die in group AoE.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG28", "2nd Boss - Exploding AoE - 3 players will receive a growing AoE circle under their feet. Take this out of the group as it will explode.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG29", "2nd Boss - Flesh Abomination - at 90% and then every 5% down to 50% you will get a Flesh Abomination summoned from a rune. Be careful to not burn the boss too fast or you will struggle to deal with the Abominations.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG30", "2nd Boss - Fire Behemoth - At 50% the Abominations stop and Fire Behemoths appear, they will crouch when they hit 0 health then explode, so be careful where the off-tank positions them. The charge that should hit the off-tank needs to be dodged.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG31", "2nd Boss - Prime Meteors - At 25% Prime Meteors will spawn on the ground, they do not have a lot of health but must take priority and be focused and killed fast or they will explode and damage the group.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG32", "Next Adds - Moving into the next area we find a new Havorcel, the Torchaster along with a Fire Behemoth. You can wait for the Fire Behemoth to walk away on his patrol route before engaging the first set of mobs to reduce the amount of damage. You will also get Butchers, Barbarians and more small adds.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG33", "Havocrel Torchcaster - He will raise his left arm and call a Prime Meteor to hit the ground, once it land it needs killing quickly or it will charge itself up and explode, wiping the group.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG34", "2nd Mini Boss - Ash Titan - The group should focus the Torchcaster first along with its Prime Meteor then deal with the Barbarian. The Ash Titan cast Molten Rain meteors that need kiting and fire circles that should be avoided. It also shoots 3 fire waves that should hit the main tank who has the mini-boss faced away from the group.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG35", "Final Boss - Xalvakka - The final boss fight takes place on 3 levels inside the main tower. At 70% and 40% you will need to follow the boss up the stairs to the next level to continue the fight.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG36", "Final Boss - Phase 1 - Scathing Evisceration - This is a set of 5 strikes that hit the tank with the initial hit being very hard. They happen fast and regularly and need to be blocked")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG37", "Final Boss - Phase 1 - Purge Soul - If you contact any of the blobs you will become infected and take damage, the longer the infection is on you the more damage you take so you need to purge using the provided synergy, do this away from the group as you will drop a new blob when you synergise.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG38", "Final Boss - Phase 1 - Portal Adds - Portals will appear at the edge of the area and adds will appear. Iron Attros which shoot fireballs, Flame Watchers, Flame Attros, Deadroths & Clanfears appear, Havorcel Goliaths will appear & needs stacking by the boss as they create a large fire AoE with a safe zone in the middle.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG39", "Final Boss - Phase 1 - Fire Waves - The boss creates a fire geyser that will send out waves of fire that are not too much of a threat and can either be healed through or avoided.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG40", "Final Boss - Phase 1 - Wraiths - These come in from the outside, if they reach the boss then the boss gains a damage shield. Any additional Wraiths that touch the shield will strengthen it so having AoEs on the boss and killing the Wraiths before they reach the boss is important.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG41", "Final Boss - Phase 1 - Deadstar Blast - This attack from the main boss will hit random players, 1 hit is survivable but 2 will oneshot most DD's if you are not blocking and well healed. Watch for the boss holding multiple fireballs above its head.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG42", "Final Boss - Phase 1 - Creeping Manifold - You can become connected to the boss via a red tether, the further away from the boss you go the less damage you will take. The tether will eventually expire and you can move back to the boss again.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG43", "Final Boss - Phase 2 - At 70% the boss will leave, you need to follow it up the stairs as the bottom floor will very quickly be filled with lava. 3 fire jets shoot out of the center column of the staircase, you can either run through and heal or wait for them to deactivate, just be aware that the lava is rising all the time.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG44", "Final Boss - Phase 2 - Volatile Shell - This floor will fill with a large fire AoE and 3 copies of the boss will appear. You need to bash the shades to work out which one is the real boss, the others can then be ignored. The same mechanics & adds from the ground floor still appear in this phase.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG45", "Final Boss - Phase 2 - Deadstar Burst - The Deadstar Blast mechanic now bounces AoE bursts before it hits players.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG46", "Final Boss - Phase 3 - At 40% the boss will head up the stairs again, ignore any remaining adds and head after it immediately. The top floor has a hole in the middle so be careful where you stand.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NRG47", "Final Boss - Phase 3 - Boss Split - The boss will split into 3 again the same as the middle floor. The same mechanic applies.")



